<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Advertisements on RaihnForge</title><link>https://RaihnForge.github.io/tags/advertisements/</link><description>Recent content in Advertisements on RaihnForge</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 10 Oct 2013 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://RaihnForge.github.io/tags/advertisements/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Collectable Supplies Coupon</title><link>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/collectable-supplies-coupon/</link><pubDate>Thu, 10 Oct 2013 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/collectable-supplies-coupon/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/collectible_supplies_discount_04.jpg"&gt;&lt;img src="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/collectible_supplies_discount_04.jpg" alt="collectible_supplies_discount_04" title="collectible_supplies_discount_04"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;I’ve been privileges enough to do some work for Collectible Supplies from time to time.  This was a very fun and challenging coupon to design, but I feel like in the end the work paid off!  Still, I feel like I could have done a better job with the message text.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h6 id="--oct-2012-design"&gt;&lt;em&gt;- Oct 2012 design&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/collectible_supplies_discount_138810.png"&gt;&lt;img src="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/collectible_supplies_discount_138810.png" alt="collectible_supplies_discount_138810" title="collectible_supplies_discount_138810"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;  Updated design Oct 2013.  Cleaned up some fonts and removed the holiday theme.
Check out &lt;a href="http://www.collectible-supplies.com/" title="http://www.collectible-supplies.com/"&gt;Collectible-Supplies.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Team Eve Gaming Logo</title><link>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/team-eve-gaming-logo/</link><pubDate>Thu, 31 May 2012 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/team-eve-gaming-logo/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/eve_logo_large.png"&gt;&lt;img src="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/eve_logo_large.png" alt="eve_logo_large" title="eve_logo_large"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Creating Team Eve’s logo was a rewarding experience, and a test of the process of achieving a shared vision with a client.  Below I discuss the process I used to communicate online, across the globe, to deliver not only a logo for an up and coming eSports team, but some working assets for their web and streaming needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PHASE 1 - INTENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/wp-imports/gamedev/1.png" alt="1"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish Intent - The above image compiled the sources that I asked the client bring to me as direction on how we might evaluate their personal tastes for their design and their intent.  I want the final product to represent as best as possible the client&amp;rsquo;s unique identity as well as resolve their professional needs.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>WIld Goose Casio Print Designs</title><link>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/wild-goose-casio-print-designs/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Mar 2011 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/wild-goose-casio-print-designs/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.joshuakeyes.us/wordpress/raihn/images/a965d3aa5f34_F61C/casino-aniversery2.png"&gt;&lt;img src="http://www.joshuakeyes.us/wordpress/raihn/images/a965d3aa5f34_F61C/casino-aniversery2_thumb.png" alt="casino aniversery2" title="casino aniversery2"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;  &lt;a href="http://www.joshuakeyes.us/wordpress/raihn/images/a965d3aa5f34_F61C/Friday-Poker-copy.png"&gt;&lt;img src="http://www.joshuakeyes.us/wordpress/raihn/images/a965d3aa5f34_F61C/Friday-Poker-copy_thumb.png" alt="Friday Poker copy" title="Friday Poker copy"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;   &lt;a href="http://www.joshuakeyes.us/wordpress/raihn/images/a965d3aa5f34_F61C/holdem_tournament-copy2.png"&gt;&lt;img src="http://www.joshuakeyes.us/wordpress/raihn/images/a965d3aa5f34_F61C/holdem_tournament-copy2_thumb.png" alt="holdem_tournament copy2" title="holdem_tournament copy2"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These assets were used for a Casino as a way to update some of the look and feel of their promotions and table print outs.  The project was far and away from what I usually work on.  In the end, though the project was very fun and I was able to learn many more interesting techniques in creating fun designs for print of online assets.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Store Coupon Created for Collectible Supplies</title><link>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/store-coupon-created-for-collectible-supplies/</link><pubDate>Sun, 10 Feb 2008 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/store-coupon-created-for-collectible-supplies/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/collectible_supplies_discount_04.jpg" alt="Store Coupon for Collectible Supplies"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Political Cartoon for Washington post</title><link>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/illustration/political-cartoon-washington-post/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Aug 2007 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/illustration/political-cartoon-washington-post/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/pctg_ad_washington_post_master.jpg"&gt;&lt;img src="https://RaihnForge.github.io/images/recovered/pctg_ad_washington_post_master.jpg" alt="pctg_ad_washington_post_master" title="pctg_ad_washington_post_master"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;    Another Ad I have illustrated in conjunction with DIP and &lt;a href="https://www.PCtheGame.com"&gt;www.PCtheGame.com&lt;/a&gt; (Politically Correct the Game) for The Washington Post. I quite enjoyed the final outcome of this project.  Political opinions aside, I just enjoy the color and mirth of the project.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Web &amp;amp; Print Advertisements for Politically Correct the Game</title><link>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/web-print-advertisements-for-politically-correct-the-game/</link><pubDate>Thu, 12 Apr 2007 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://RaihnForge.github.io/art/branding/web-print-advertisements-for-politically-correct-the-game/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disclaimer&lt;/strong&gt;
